  "final": "`get_document` and `list_documents` now only return documents that match both the tenant and the owner and haven't been deleted. Both the existing check and a new one I added pass.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`src/repository.py`**: `find` and `listing` now take `tenant` and `owner`. They only return rows where `tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL`, and every value is passed as a bound parameter. `listing` used to filter by owner only, so it could return documents from other tenants.\n- **`src/service.py`**: passes `tenant` and `owner` through to those functions.\n- **Unchanged:** results still contain only `id`, `title` and `body`, lists are still sorted by id, and `get_document` returns `None` for any ID you can't access. It gives the same `None` whether the document is missing, deleted, or belongs to another tenant or owner.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 checks/public.py` passes.\n- The new `checks/access.py` passes. It checks that deleted, cross-tenant, cross-owner and missing IDs all return `None`, and that lists are sorted by id and leave out documents the caller can't access. It also checks that tenant and owner names containing quotes work normally, and that injection-style strings like `t' OR '1'='1` return nothing.\n\nThe signatures of `find` and `listing` changed. In this project only `src/service.py` calls them, but any other code that calls them directly would need updating.",
